    "us-policy-positions:health-human-services.work-requirement-for-assistance": {
      "source": "Public Law 119-21 (the 2025 budget reconciliation law), per KFF and CHCS summaries: SNAP work rules widened (ages 55 to 64; parents of children 14 and older) from Nov. 1, 2025. Georgia's Pathways since July 1, 2023 applies to Medicaid, not food or income assistance, and is under the Medicaid question.",
      "note": "The federal law answers yes for every place.",
